/-!
# The Behrend–Fantechi virtual fundamental class: target signatures

**This file is not the roadmap and is not exhaustive.** The definitive document is `README.md`.
No headline statement can be written using the pinned carriers. Tau Ceti supplies
`SchPseudofunctor`, `Spaces.IsAlgebraicSpace` and scheme-level `Chow.ChowGroup`.

* End goal 1, the intrinsic cone (§5.4; Behrend–Fantechi Thm. 3.11), needs
  Deligne–Mumford stacks, geometric cotangent complexes and cone stacks.
* End goal 2, obstruction theories (§6.1; Behrend–Fantechi Thm. 4.5 for the
  deformation criterion), needs geometric cotangent complexes and the dual cone construction.
* End goal 3, the virtual class (§§7.1–7.4; Behrend–Fantechi Def. 5.2 and Prop. 5.3),
  needs resolved cones, rational stack Chow groups and zero-section Gysin.
* End goal 4, the formulas (§§7.5–8.4; Behrend–Fantechi Props. 5.5–5.10), needs
  the virtual class and its refined Gysin and product operations.
* End goal 5, the relative class (Layer 9; Behrend–Fantechi §7), needs relative
  cones, cotangent complexes over algebraic bases and their Chow operations.
* End goal 6, the public class (§7.4), needs evaluation on a resolution and
  the independence theorem for that evaluation.
-/

